# Stock Data Service v0.0.0.4 - NYSE Arca Support

## Date: 2026-02-15

### Issue Fixed: NYSE Arca Ticker Update Problem

#### Problem Description:
1. NYSE Arca tickers (like SPY) were not being updated even though they were present in nysearca_tickers.json
2. The ticker list was being downloaded by sync_nyse.py but not used by the main application

#### Root Cause:
The main application (main.py) only synchronized NASDAQ and NYSE tickers. It completely ignored NYSE Arca tickers, even though the yahoo_finance.py module had the capability to fetch them.

#### Solution Implemented:
Updated main.py to include NYSE Arca tickers in the synchronization process:

1. Modified run_sync() method:
   - Added Step 1c to fetch NYSE Arca tickers using get_nysearca_tickers()
   - Updated ticker combination logic to include NYSE Arca
   - Updated logging to reflect NYSE Arca ticker retrieval

2. Updated documentation:
   - Updated module docstring to reflect v0.0.0.4 and mention NYSE Arca support
   - Updated run_sync() docstring to specify all three exchanges

#### Impact:
- NYSE Arca tickers (including SPY, QQQ, and other ETFs) will now be:
  - Downloaded and tracked like NASDAQ and NYSE tickers
  - Updated daily with historical data
  - Properly maintained in the database

#### Files Modified:
- main.py - Added NYSE Arca ticker synchronization

#### How It Works Now:
1. When the main sync runs (via main.py), it:
   - Fetches NASDAQ tickers
   - Fetches NYSE tickers  
   - Fetches NYSE Arca tickers (NEW)
   - Combines all three into one set
   - Identifies new vs. existing tickers
   - Processes new tickers (downloads full 10-year history)
   - Updates existing tickers (fetches latest data)

2. The sync_nyse.py script can still be run separately to:
   - Download NYSE and NYSE Arca ticker lists
   - Add new tickers from these exchanges to the database
   - Save ticker lists to JSON files for reference

